vm-4 — Code generation: core forms (plan-2-bytecode-vm).

Emit bytecode for the everyday special operators + calls.

WHAT (compile <form> in an analyzed compile-env -> bytecode, tracking stack depth)
- self-evaluating / QUOTE -> PUSH-CONST (add literal to the constant pool, dedup).
- variable ref -> LOAD-LOCAL depth idx (lexical) or LOAD-GLOBAL sym (special/global).
- (f a1..an) -> compile args left-to-right, then CALL-NAMED f n (or compile the
  function form + CALL n).  Tail position -> TAIL-CALL (for loops-as-recursion).
- IF -> compile test, JUMP-IF-NIL else, then-branch, JUMP end, else-branch.
- PROGN -> compile each, DROP all but last (respect value/effect context).
- LET / LET* -> evaluate inits, bind into fresh local slots (LET evaluates all
  inits before binding; LET* sequentially); SPECIAL vars use a dynamic-bind opcode
  + UNWIND on exit.
- SETQ -> compile value, STORE-LOCAL / STORE-GLOBAL, leave value on stack.
- FUNCTION -> LOAD-FUNCTION sym, or MAKE-CLOSURE for a local lambda (vm-6).
- THE -> compile the sub-form (optionally emit a type check).
- LAMBDA at top -> compile to a compiled-function template.
- VALUE vs EFFECT vs TAIL context threaded through codegen so unused values are
  dropped and tail calls emitted.

ACCEPTANCE: compile+run a battery: arithmetic, nested LET/LET*, IF chains, a
countdown loop, SETQ, calling built-ins and other compiled fns; compare to the
tree-walker on the same inputs.

DEPENDS ON: vm-2 (to run), vm-3 (analysis).
